ain.\n- **Neurological:** Occasional headaches, no numbness or tingling in extremities.\n- **Musculoskeletal:** Carpal tunnel release 2 years ago, no issues reported.\n- **Psychiatric:** History of depression, currently managed.\n\n**2. Objective:**\n\n**Physical Examination:**\n- **General:** Alert, oriented, well-nourished.\n- **Vital Signs:** Blood pressure elevated in office setting.\n- **Cardiovascular:** Regular rate and rhythm, no murmurs.\n- **Respiratory:** Clear to auscultation bilaterally.\n- **Neurological:** No focal deficits, strength 5/5 bilaterally.\n- **Musculoskeletal:** No tenderness or swelling, carpal tunnel release well-healed.\n- **Psychiatric:** Cooperative, no evidence of depression or anxiety.\n\n**Investigation/Test Results:**\n- Blood Pressure: Elevated in office setting.\n- Labs: Results pending for CBC, CMP, and Lipid Panel.\n\n**3. Assessment:**\n1. Hypertension - Uncontrolled.\n2. Depression - Well-managed.\n3. Carpal Tunnel Release - History of, no current issues.\n\n**4. Plan:**\n1. **Hypertension:**\n   - Increase Lisinopril to 10 mg/day, oral, once daily.\n   - Monitor blood pressure at home.\n   - Follow-up in 1 month to reassess blood pressure control.\n\n2. **Depression:**\n   - Continue current medication regimen.\n   - Weekly therapy sessions to continue.\n\n3. **Carpal Tunnel Release:**\n   - No current issues reported.\n\n**Patient Agreements:**\nThe patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ Dax: Good morning, Christine. So I know my nurse told you a little bit of-... um, about dax and I\'m gon na tell dax a little bit about you, if that\'s okay?\nPatient: Go for it.\nDax: Okay, great. um, uh, this is christine. she\'s a 63-year-old female patient. you\'re here for your routine, um, yearly exam. um, i know you have a history of high blood pressure and you\'ve had some depression in the past. and i also know you did have a carpal tunnel release done about t